# Copy to .env.local. Nothing here is secret except the key.

# ── Where the text goes (§5) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The question that decides everything. Answer it before anyone puts real client
# material in the box. One module honours these: lib/ai/provider.ts
#
#   anthropic  the first-party API (default)
#   bedrock    AWS Bedrock, under the firm's existing AWS agreement
#   vertex     Google Vertex AI
#   foundry    Microsoft Foundry
VIRTUS_AI_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Required when VIRTUS_AI_PROVIDER=anthropic.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# The firm's classification line, said plainly by /api/where and in the footer
# rather than discovered during a security review.
VIRTUS_CLASSIFICATION=Internal, non-confidential or public use only. No Restricted material.

# ── Who can open it ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A shared code, so a forwarded URL is not an open door. Leave it unset and
# there is no gate at all — which is what you want locally, and lesson 12.10:
# fail open on a gate that can lock you out.
#
# Not identity. It says "you were told the code" and nothing about who you are.
VIRTUS_PASSCODE=

# A second code, for changing what everybody sees: broadcasts, the house style,
# the organisation model, and templates built in the admin space. Separate from
# the one above on purpose — "you were told the code to get in" is the right
# size for reading and the wrong size for editing a strip that appears on every
# screen in the firm.
#
# Unset means open, exactly as above. The Admin screen then says out loud that
# anybody can change it, rather than letting somebody assume otherwise.
VIRTUS_ADMIN_PASSCODE=

# ── Where what the firm shares is kept ────────────────────────────────────────
# Broadcasts, the house style, the organisation model and admin-built templates
# are the firm's, not one laptop's. Set this and they are kept in one place and
# reach every device. Leave it unset and they stay in whichever browser set
# them — which is what a local checkout wants, and what the Admin screen says.
#
# Create a Blob store in the Vercel dashboard and this variable is injected for
# you. Personal work — notes, drafts, finished documents — is never kept here.
#
# For running the shared path locally, `file:` followed by a path uses a file on
# disk instead. Never in production: a serverless filesystem is ephemeral and
# would forget everything between requests.
#
#   BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=file:./.virtus-shared.json
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# ── Models ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both passes default to claude-opus-5. The structure pass is a candidate for a
# cheaper model once you have measured what it costs you — that is a per-firm
# decision, which is why it is a variable and not a hardcoded downgrade.
VIRTUS_MODEL_STRUCTURE=claude-opus-5
VIRTUS_MODEL_OUTLINE=claude-opus-5

# ── Deck ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Footer on every slide.
VIRTUS_DECK_FOOTER=Internal
